Author: anthnel <anthoni.devops@proton.me>
Date:   Tue Nov 24 18:15:29 2026 +0100

    fix(scan): pass chart and overlay folders as paths so a dash-named folder is never an option (DEVDESK-763)

    Folder names come from the scanned repository. One starting with '-'
    (--load-restrictor=LoadRestrictionsNone, -x) was passed bare to kustomize
    build, helm lint and helm template and read as an option; a manifest file
    named like an option reached kubeconform the same way.

    helmArgs and kustomizeArgs now pass such a folder as ./<name>; kubeconform
    gets -- before its files when one starts with '-'. Ordinary names keep their
    exact argv, and findings, steps and Repro keep the folder's own name.
    Discovery keeps these folders; the behavior is covered and documented in
    scanning.md.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 6f5373107e94

